<p>A three-judge panel of the 5th U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals temporarily blocked the Food and Drug Administration’s 2023 policy allowing mifepristone, a drug used in medication abortions, to be prescribed by telemedicine and delivered by mail nationwide. The New Orleans-based court said patients must obtain the drug in person, a ruling that applies in states that ban abortion and in states where it remains legal. Louisiana brought the case, arguing that the FDA policy allowed out-of-state prescribers to send mifepristone into the state despite its abortion laws. The panel ruled that the regulation undermined Louisiana’s abortion laws and caused the state irreparable harm; Politico reported that two judges on the panel were appointed by President Trump and one by President George W. Bush. The decision reversed a lower-court order that had allowed mail delivery to continue while the FDA reviewed its mifepristone rules. Danco Laboratories, one of the companies distributing mifepristone in the United States, said it planned to seek emergency relief from the Supreme Court.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TsBA0LgTHOpptXudIXWOP4fQqy8HQcH98R9PzulhCpx8At57vgczK7Aof1mYTn0Cxyw2giUIIE7Pc2t1_0G_EuPoZ8aKRRGOLyPHX5jwI0MUPP-m1oZPALRchSr-ixMwsGiWSdYGm7Ml8H188surZg8FnX5Y_L9LVQ4JvMmFvLCgdknXyGYqN_8wNVaN8mWHKj0G72Vx2FFt47d6FEdjNjSv5RcRGppJZQqCtOb1FQEJvHgnKpht--jgZw' alt='Mifepristone tablets at a Planned Parenthood clinic in Iowa, July 18, 2024.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Common method: Medication abortions using mifepristone and misoprostol accounted for 63% of U.S. abortions in 2023, according to the Guttmacher Institute figure cited by EWTN News.</li><li>Miscarriage care: Mifepristone is also used in the management of early miscarriages.</li><li>State access: About 20 states now ban or restrict abortion.</li></ul><blockquote>Anti-abortion politicians have just made it much harder for people everywhere in the country to get a medication that abortion and miscarriage patients have been safely using for more than 25 years - Julia Kaye</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Louisiana: The state argued the Biden-era mifepristone rules threatened its sovereignty and the safety of pregnant women. Politico reported that the panel ruled unanimously in Louisiana’s favor. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/01/appeals-court-approves-sweeping-abortion-pill-restrictions-teeing-up-scotus-showdown-00903298'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Michigan Gov. Gretchen Whitmer: The governor condemned the ruling as a “dangerous, partisan attempt to erode reproductive freedom.” (<a href='https://www.wlns.com/news/politics/governor-whitmer-condemns-telehealth-ruling/'>WLNS</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/court-restricts-abortion-access-across-us-by-blocking-mailing-of-mifepristone/article70930789.ece'>Court restricts abortion access across U.S. by blocking mailing of mifepristone</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/02/us-court-temporarily-blocks-access-to-abortion-pills-by-mail_6753051_4.html'>US court temporarily blocks access to abortion pills by mail</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-appeals-court-temporarily-halts-mail-delivery-of-abortion-pill'>US appeals court temporarily halts mail delivery of abortion pill</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c2k20z5yj3wo'>US court limits mail-order access to abortion pill mifepristone</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/01/appeals-court-approves-sweeping-abortion-pill-restrictions-teeing-up-scotus-showdown-00903298'>US appeals court approves sweeping abortion pill restrictions, teeing up high court showdown</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.king5.com/article/news/nation-world/a-court-has-restricted-abortion-access-across-the-us-by-blocking-mailing-prescri